1
00:05:31,199 --> 00:05:37,199
Free your mind.

2
00:11:02,399 --> 00:11:08,399
The Matrix Reloaded is a adventure, action,
thriller film directed by Lana Wachowski.

3
00:16:33,599 --> 00:16:39,599
The Resistance builds in numbers as humans are freed from
the Matrix and brought to the city of Zion.

4
00:22:04,799 --> 00:22:10,799
Neo discovers his superpowers, including the ability
to see the code inside the Matrix.

5
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:42,000
With machine sentinels digging to Zion in 72 hours, Neo, Morpheus and
Trinity must find the Keymaker to ultimately reach the Source.

6
00:33:07,199 --> 00:33:13,199
Neo, played by Keanu Reeves.

7
00:38:38,400 --> 00:38:44,400
Morpheus, played by Laurence Fishburne.

8
00:44:09,599 --> 00:44:15,599
Trinity, played by Carrie-Anne Moss.

9
00:49:40,799 --> 00:49:46,799
Agent Smith, played by Hugo Weaving.

10
00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
Niobe, played by Jada Pinkett Smith.

11
01:00:43,199 --> 01:00:49,199
The Oracle, played by Gloria Foster.

12
01:06:14,399 --> 01:06:20,399
The Matrix Reloaded is a 2003 American science fiction action
film written and directed by the Wachowskis.

13
01:11:45,599 --> 01:11:51,599
It is the sequel to The Matrix (1999) and the second
installment in the Matrix film series.

14
01:17:16,800 --> 01:17:22,800
The film stars Keanu Reeves, Laurence Fishburne, Carrie-Anne Moss, Hugo Weaving, and Gloria Foster who
reprise their roles from the previous film, with Jada Pinkett Smith joining the cast.

15
01:22:48,000 --> 01:22:54,000
In the film, Neo, Morpheus, and Trinity attempt to reach the Source of the Matrix
to end the war as Zion prepares for an invasion from the machines.

16
01:28:19,199 --> 01:28:25,199
The film premiered on May 7, 2003, in Westwood, Los Angeles,
California, and had its worldwide release by Warner Bros.

17
01:33:50,399 --> 01:33:56,399
Pictures on May 15, 2003, including a screening out of
competition at the 2003 Cannes Film Festival.

18
01:39:21,599 --> 01:39:27,599
The video game Enter the Matrix and The Animatrix, a collection of
short animations, supported and expanded the film's story.

19
01:44:52,800 --> 01:44:58,800
The film received generally positive reviews, though most
critics found it inferior to the first film.

20
01:50:24,000 --> 01:50:30,000
It grossed $741.8 million worldwide, breaking Terminator 2: Judgment Day's record for becoming the
highest-grossing R-rated film of all time, until Deadpool surpassed it in 2016.

21
01:55:55,199 --> 01:56:01,199
In addition to being the highest-grossing film in the franchise, it was the third-highest-grossing
film of 2003, behind The Lord of the Rings: The Return of the King and Finding Nemo.

22
02:01:26,399 --> 02:01:32,399
A direct sequel titled The Matrix Revolutions was
released six months later on November 5, 2003.

23
02:06:57,599 --> 02:07:03,599
The film explores themes of dying and death, future,
mission, man vs machine, underground world.

24
02:12:28,799 --> 02:12:34,799
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
